  "question": {
    "text": "Let $C_1$ be the circle in the third quadrant of radius 3 , that touches both coordinate axes. Let $\\mathrm{C}_2$ be the circle with centre $(1,3)$ that touches $\\mathrm{C}_1$ externally at the point $(\\alpha, \\beta)$. If $(\\beta-\\alpha)^2=\\frac{m}{n}, \\operatorname{gcd}(m, n)=1$, then $m+n$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "9",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "13",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "22",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "31",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$C_1:(x+3)^2+(y+3)^2=3^2$<br/><img src=\"assets\\st0000_77fdf61bb4b3.png\"/><br/>Let $\\mathrm{C}_1$ and $\\mathrm{C}_2$ has centres $A\\left(-3_1-3\\right)$ and $B(1,3)$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{AB}=\\sqrt{16+36}=2 \\sqrt{13} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}_1=3 \\text { and } \\mathrm{r}_2=2 \\sqrt{13}-3 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P}(\\alpha, \\beta), \\alpha=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1(1)+\\mathrm{r}_2(-3)}{\\mathrm{r}_1+\\mathrm{r}_2}, \\beta=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1(3)+\\mathrm{r}_2(-3)}{\\mathrm{r}_1+\\mathrm{r}_2} \\\\\n& \\alpha=\\frac{3-3(2 \\sqrt{13}-3)}{2 \\sqrt{13}}, \\beta=\\frac{18-6 \\sqrt{13}}{2 \\sqrt{13}} \\\\\n& (\\beta-\\alpha)^2=\\left(\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{13}}\\right)^2 \\\\\n& (\\beta-\\alpha)^2=\\left(\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{13}}\\right)^2, \\mathrm{~m}+\\mathrm{n}=22<br/>\\end{aligned}$"
  }
